    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18480" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφρά̆δ-μων</span></b> , in Trag. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφράσμων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφραδής</span>
			, c. inf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφράδμονες
				προγνώμεναι</span>
			<i>without sense</i> to foresee, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				256
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναικὸς ὡς ἀφράσμονος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1401
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				613
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφρασμόνως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					417
				</span></i>
			.—Only poet.</div>
